472
00:29:32,700 --> 00:29:35,660
And is there a possibility it might go off in error?

473
00:29:36,020 --> 00:29:40,400
Since their inception, the technology behind the air bag has been greatly refined.

474
00:29:40,401 --> 00:29:43,500
They are truly an amazing piece of engineering.

475
00:29:44,360 --> 00:29:49,720
When sensors ascertain a collision force equal to running into a brick wall at 10 to 15 miles an hour,

476
00:29:50,280 --> 00:29:55,300
nitrogen gas is produced and fills the nylon airbag at a speed of up to 200 miles an hour

477
00:29:55,301 --> 00:29:58,780
and within one 50th of a second of sensing the crash.

478
00:29:59,040 --> 00:30:03,080
When they worked and the engineer said it's go time, we made them standard.

479
00:30:03,360 --> 00:30:05,100
We didn't fool around. We just implemented them.

480
00:30:05,101 --> 00:30:10,320
In the next 50 years, I would imagine that all cars will have

481
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:14,180
whether it'll be airbags or some other, some type of interior safety system

482
00:30:14,181 --> 00:30:17,960
to protect the occupant from impacts in any direction,

483
00:30:18,640 --> 00:30:21,200
whether from the rear, front, or side, or even rollovers.

484
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:24,880
Safety has gone from being almost a taboo subject

485
00:30:24,881 --> 00:30:29,960
to being not only mainstream, but actually attractive to a lot of manufacturers and a lot of cars.

486
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:38,640
This sporty little red car is a rolling safety laboratory.

487
00:30:38,641 --> 00:30:42,940
Volvo calls it the SCC or safety concept car.

488
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:46,600
It's packed with technology you'll be seeing in your car in the future.

489
00:30:47,520 --> 00:30:49,000
The technology will be transparent.

490
00:30:49,380 --> 00:30:51,360
It'll just enhance the driving experience.

491
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:54,900
The forward collision warning radar tells your cruise control

492
00:30:54,901 --> 00:30:56,880
when you're getting too close too quickly.

493
00:30:57,100 --> 00:31:00,720
Maybe you're getting drowsy and you're all of a sudden approaching a vehicle very close.

494
00:31:01,180 --> 00:31:04,740
We will have a system that will alert you audibly and visually.

495
00:31:05,340 --> 00:31:08,620
But as you proceed towards this vehicle, we may start applying the brain.

496
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:15,640
If the sensors no longer detect the vehicle in front, your car would accelerate back to its selected speed.

497
00:31:15,641 --> 00:31:20,640
The lane-changing aids senses when someone is approaching in your blind spot in the next lane

498
00:31:20,641 --> 00:31:23,640
and let you know before you make a mistake.

499
00:31:23,641 --> 00:31:30,640
And there are cameras all over the car to better see your side angles directly behind you,

500
00:31:30,641 --> 00:31:32,640
and what your kids are up to.

501
00:31:32,641 --> 00:31:37,640
What we want to create is a car that there's no surprise is when you move around a situation.

502
00:31:37,641 --> 00:31:44,540
The SCC is designed specifically to help you see out of the car better.

503
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:47,240
The unique feature is that when you sit in the car,

504
00:31:47,360 --> 00:31:49,660
there's an eye sensor that looks for the whites of your eyes

505
00:31:49,661 --> 00:31:55,280
and brings the seat up to a position that we know is the best for you to be able to see out of the car.

506
00:31:55,840 --> 00:31:58,360
Everything will adjust to your perfect driving position.

507
00:31:58,840 --> 00:32:02,840
The seat, the floor pedals, the steering wheel, and even the gear shift.

508
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:05,780
Once in position, blind spots will disappear.

509
00:32:05,781 --> 00:32:07,620
What is known as the A-pillar,

510
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:10,020
is partially transparent so you can see through it.

511
00:32:10,520 --> 00:32:12,420
The usual over-the-shoulder blind spot

512
00:32:12,421 --> 00:32:15,700
caused by the B pillar is also reduced by 25%

513
00:32:15,701 --> 00:32:17,700
because the pillars bend inward.

514
00:32:18,420 --> 00:32:21,680
Such a design also adds protection in a rollover accident.

515
00:32:22,720 --> 00:32:24,800
The advanced light system uses sensors

516
00:32:24,801 --> 00:32:27,740
to automatically adjust headlights to changes in the road.

517
00:32:28,300 --> 00:32:30,140
And the active night vision system

518
00:32:30,141 --> 00:32:31,820
will help you see in the dark

519
00:32:31,821 --> 00:32:34,940
and prepare the car to react before you do.

520
00:32:35,180 --> 00:32:37,520
The next stage of the active night vision system

521
00:32:37,521 --> 00:32:40,440
where I could see with clarity what's happening on the roadway.

522
00:32:40,740 --> 00:32:43,060
Now can I analyze what's happening on the roadway

523
00:32:43,061 --> 00:32:44,540
and then warn the driver similarly

524
00:32:44,541 --> 00:32:47,260
and then control some of the safety features we have inside the vehicle.

525
00:32:47,920 --> 00:32:52,660
The experimental F-400 carving is Mercedes Rolling Laboratory.

526
00:32:53,500 --> 00:32:55,540
The name carving says it all.

527
00:32:56,060 --> 00:32:59,500
It's like a slalom skier carving turns down a tight course.

528
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:04,440
Its main safety feature is its steering system called active camber control.

529
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:07,360
When cornering, the car's outer wheels

530
00:33:07,361 --> 00:33:13,400
lean into the bend at an angle up to 20 degrees, increasing stability and reducing the danger of spinning.

531
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:22,940
The tilt angle is controlled by a drive-by-wire system, which measures speed, acceleration, steering turning, and lateral forces.

532
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:32,760
Then, its active hydronomatic system optimizes the suspension and shock absorption in line with a changing situation on the road, all at lightning speed.

533
00:33:32,761 --> 00:33:35,640
It also uses special tires that are asymmetrical,

534
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:39,260
which means the inner area of the tread is slightly rounded off.

535
00:33:39,760 --> 00:33:42,760
When driving straight ahead, the outer tread meets the road.

536
00:33:43,320 --> 00:33:45,940
When turning, the inner tread is in contact.

537
00:33:46,760 --> 00:33:52,320
Mercedes says the system improves lateral force by as much as 30% to 1.3Gs.

538
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:56,160
It all adds up to handling, cornering at higher speeds,

539
00:33:56,500 --> 00:33:58,240
more like a motorcycle than a car.

540
00:33:59,180 --> 00:34:00,400
One thing is clear.

541
00:34:01,140 --> 00:34:02,500
A high-tech car of the future.

542
00:34:02,760 --> 00:34:05,180
will do everything it can to make our lives safer.

543
00:34:05,780 --> 00:34:08,080
But will we be giving it too much responsibility?

544
00:34:08,540 --> 00:34:10,760
The driver is really the most important safety feature.

545
00:34:10,860 --> 00:34:11,620
We can do a lot.

546
00:34:12,020 --> 00:34:14,040
We can add more and more technology, but it's the driver.

547
00:34:14,460 --> 00:34:16,680
I think there was a natural backlash

548
00:34:16,681 --> 00:34:19,540
to giving over too much control to technology.

549
00:34:20,340 --> 00:34:24,600
We like technology to offer us conveniences and safety measures,

550
00:34:25,140 --> 00:34:29,620
but I don't think very many people yet are ready to sort of turn over control of the vehicle

551
00:34:29,621 --> 00:34:31,940
to a microprocessor and just become a passenger.

552
00:34:31,941 --> 00:34:36,340
We like to drive. If we didn't, we could take a bus, take a train, take a plane.

553
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:49,600
The National Highway Safety Administration estimates that in the U.S., the seatbelt saves over 4,000 lives

554
00:34:49,601 --> 00:34:53,180
and prevents over 100,000 injuries each year.

555
00:34:53,900 --> 00:34:57,660
Modern Marvel's car take of the future will return on the History Channel.

556
00:35:01,940 --> 00:35:07,600
There are cars, and then there are sports cars.

557
00:35:09,980 --> 00:35:12,580
Close to the ground, wind in your face.

558
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:16,060
The world seems to have a love affair with the sports car.

559
00:35:17,620 --> 00:35:20,280
Sports cars are meant to be driven,

560
00:35:20,640 --> 00:35:23,480
as opposed to passenger cars, which are meant to be ridden in.

561
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:27,640
These are cars that, theoretically, their entire purpose

562
00:35:27,641 --> 00:35:30,520
is to entertain the driver and one very lucky passenger.

563
00:35:30,521 --> 00:35:40,220
There's a lust factor, frankly, that you want to connect with, a certain freedom, a youthfulness, a time of life, an attitude toward life.

564
00:35:40,560 --> 00:35:49,240
Brands like Mustang, Corvette, Thunderbird, come to symbolize something in all of our psyches, and that really doesn't go away.

565
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:55,140
But it's not just about fun.

566
00:35:55,900 --> 00:35:59,420
Sports cars play an important role in the future of car technology.

567
00:35:59,421 --> 00:36:04,960
Since 1904, when Mercedes turned its first race car into a road car,

568
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:08,940
cutting-edge innovations have been trickling down from the racetrack,

569
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:13,520
going first into sports cars, and finally into regular passenger vehicles.

570
00:36:13,521 --> 00:36:19,580
The role of motorsport has been an immense provocator of technology improvement.

571
00:36:19,940 --> 00:36:23,440
Their engineers are in that gymnasium that's called motorsports.

572
00:36:23,840 --> 00:36:29,180
They're being exercised right up to the last 10th or millisecond to gain speed.

573
00:36:29,420 --> 00:36:33,260
in handling, in power and transmission, in electronics,

574
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:35,760
and traction control, and braking efficiency,

575
00:36:36,140 --> 00:36:38,160
and everything that's related to the motor vehicle.

576
00:36:40,500 --> 00:36:44,220
Probably the biggest inroads of racing technology

577
00:36:44,221 --> 00:36:47,080
into traditional passenger vehicles is in the tires.

578
00:36:48,100 --> 00:36:50,160
Passenger car tires used to be really bad.

579
00:36:50,460 --> 00:36:53,080
How often you get blowouts and flats all the time,

580
00:36:53,620 --> 00:36:57,100
you go around a corner relatively slow and you hear the tires squeal.

581
00:36:57,101 --> 00:37:04,860
So today's passenger car tires are actually as good as race car tires were 20 years ago.

582
00:37:05,860 --> 00:37:10,260
Race cars exert tremendous gravitational forces and heat at high speeds.

583
00:37:10,940 --> 00:37:15,560
So tire makers have developed synthetic compounds that have excellent performance characteristics

584
00:37:15,561 --> 00:37:17,460
in a variety of racing situations.

585
00:37:18,280 --> 00:37:22,960
Furthermore, tread designs have been customized for dry or wet track conditions.

586
00:37:23,880 --> 00:37:27,080
Racing teams must choose the right tire for a particular track.

587
00:37:27,100 --> 00:37:29,060
and weather conditions on a given race day.

588
00:37:29,900 --> 00:37:32,800
Like so many factors in racing, it's a science.

589
00:37:33,820 --> 00:37:37,660
Race cars have advanced aerodynamics,

590
00:37:38,240 --> 00:37:39,940
and a lot of the lessons learned

591
00:37:39,941 --> 00:37:41,400
from developing those aerodynamics

592
00:37:41,401 --> 00:37:42,440
had been passed on

593
00:37:42,441 --> 00:37:45,420
to traditional passenger cars of today.

594
00:37:46,060 --> 00:37:47,320
Other things that come from racing

595
00:37:47,321 --> 00:37:49,320
are these onboard diagnostic computers

596
00:37:49,321 --> 00:37:52,680
that are continuously monitoring the functions of our cars.

597
00:37:52,681 --> 00:37:54,520
That kind of started out

598
00:37:54,521 --> 00:37:57,080
as the crew chief sitting on the...

599
00:37:57,100 --> 00:38:03,340
on the side of the track with telemetry monitoring what's going on in the engine of that race car to keep track of that.

600
00:38:07,500 --> 00:38:13,120
While many production car manufacturers have participated in racing with varying degrees of success,

601
00:38:13,840 --> 00:38:17,060
fewer names are synonymous with both race and street cars.

602
00:38:17,760 --> 00:38:21,800
Perhaps none personify this idea more than the name Ferrari.

603
00:38:27,100 --> 00:38:31,100
Company founder Enzo Ferrari was relentless in his quest for perfection.

604
00:38:31,880 --> 00:38:33,320
He was single-minded.

605
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:39,560
He was almost autocratic when it came to ruling his domain, his Ferrari empire.

606
00:38:40,220 --> 00:38:45,320
Like many manufacturers before him, Enzo Ferrari took advances learn from his race cars

607
00:38:45,321 --> 00:38:47,420
and incorporated them into his sports cars.

608
00:38:48,200 --> 00:38:49,900
His methods followed a new axiom.

609
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:51,300
Race on Sunday.

610
00:38:51,820 --> 00:38:52,760
Sell on Monday.

611
00:38:53,740 --> 00:38:55,420
He was a nut for racing.

612
00:38:55,421 --> 00:38:58,660
wanted to use racing to promote his cars,

613
00:38:59,120 --> 00:39:01,800
built cars principally for racing first,

614
00:39:01,920 --> 00:39:03,720
and then sold them to the public

615
00:39:03,721 --> 00:39:05,980
mostly as a way to fund his racing activities.

616
00:39:05,981 --> 00:39:07,800
That created a terribly attractive

617
00:39:07,801 --> 00:39:10,260
set of reasons for wanting a Ferrari.

618
00:39:10,680 --> 00:39:12,280
People who buy Ferraris now,

619
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:13,580
in a very real sense,

620
00:39:13,740 --> 00:39:17,360
are buying in to Ferrari's Formula One racing activities

621
00:39:17,361 --> 00:39:19,420
because the two really do go together.

622
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:25,400
Ferraris' ladies,

623
00:39:25,420 --> 00:39:33,600
bid for supercar supremacy is the Formula One-inspired Ferrari Enzo, a 660 horsepower V12 rocket

624
00:39:33,601 --> 00:39:40,260
that bursts from 0 to 60 in 3.1 seconds and has a top speed of over 200 miles per hour.

625
00:39:41,260 --> 00:39:47,160
Just as aerodynamics dominate their Formula One car designs, the Enzo's form follows the same function,

626
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:50,740
to pierce through the atmosphere with the least resistance.

627
00:39:51,780 --> 00:39:55,400
Ferrari engineers had designed the car to be aerodynamically stuously.

628
00:39:55,420 --> 00:39:56,120
stable.

629
00:39:56,121 --> 00:40:00,860
They've used extensive wind tunnel tests to maximize airflow in order to optimize

630
00:40:00,861 --> 00:40:02,334
down draft and drag forces.

631
00:40:02,335 --> 00:40:06,100
They've also borrowed electronic shifting controls from their Formula

632
00:40:06,101 --> 00:40:10,760
1 cars that are mounted on the steering wheel, so the driver's hands are kept where they're needed

633
00:40:10,761 --> 00:40:11,461
most.

634
00:40:11,462 --> 00:40:15,900
And the steering wheel even displays the tachometer's readings in a series of LEDs.

635
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:21,380
The Enzo is as close to the Ferrari Formula 1 driving experience as an owner can get.

636
00:40:22,220 --> 00:40:25,140
The price tag, a cool $660,000.

637
00:40:25,420 --> 00:40:30,700
And then there is the Porsche.

638
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:36,220
Dr. Ferdinand Porsche is credited with creating the Volkswagen Beetle in the 1930s.

639
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:40,260
But his first namesake cars didn't debut until 1946.

640
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:44,680
Since then, Porsche has built its reputation on its road cars.

641
00:40:45,140 --> 00:40:49,780
First, the 356, then the 9-11, among others, as well as its race cars.

642
00:40:50,180 --> 00:40:53,480
Many times the winner of endurance races at Le Mans and Daytona.

643
00:40:53,481 --> 00:41:01,260
While the company's flagship has been the 9-11 turbo, a brand-new Porsche supercar has joined the ranks, the Carrera GT.

644
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:07,460
The Carrera GT represents the epitome of the company's illustrious track record for technical innovation.

645
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:13,440
Like the 9-11 turbo, the Carrera GT could compete in a racetrack with few modifications.

646
00:41:14,200 --> 00:41:22,820
Its suspension is tight, its center of gravity low, its carbon fiber body very lightweight, and its aerodynamics maximized.

647
00:41:23,480 --> 00:41:25,480
The sheer spoiler is signature Porsche.

648
00:41:25,481 --> 00:41:29,480
It can be electronically raised for maximum downforce at high speeds.

649
00:41:29,481 --> 00:41:31,480
Combined with its integrated front spoiler,

650
00:41:31,481 --> 00:41:34,480
which keeps the front end from lifting at top speeds,

651
00:41:34,481 --> 00:41:41,480
the Carrera GT makes the most of its 5.5-liter 560 horsepower V10 engine.

652
00:41:41,481 --> 00:41:42,480
Top speed?

653
00:41:42,481 --> 00:41:46,480
A breathtaking, 205 miles per hour.

654
00:41:46,481 --> 00:41:50,480
To slow down, Porsche has given the car its ceramic composite brakes.

655
00:41:50,481 --> 00:41:53,480
The ceramic brake disc is especially treated

656
00:41:53,481 --> 00:41:57,480
treated carbon fiber material, cross-drilled and internally vented.

657
00:41:57,481 --> 00:42:00,480
The brake pad is a composite material.

658
00:42:00,481 --> 00:42:04,480
Together, they greatly reduce heat generated from hard braking

659
00:42:04,481 --> 00:42:07,480
and have optimum resistance to brake fade.

660
00:42:07,481 --> 00:42:13,480
Of course, all this technology as well as its pedigree has just as impressive a price tag.

661
00:42:13,481 --> 00:42:15,480
$440,000.

662
00:42:15,481 --> 00:42:20,480
In its first year, Porsche plans to build only 1,500 Carrera GTs.

663
00:42:20,481 --> 00:42:26,300
Champion driver Steve Selene,

664
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:31,640
whose Irvine California company has built its reputation racing and customizing Mustangs

665
00:42:31,641 --> 00:42:34,960
and competition cars

666
00:42:34,961 --> 00:42:39,120
is now building his own version of the car of the future.

667
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:48,280
The $360,000 Saline S7 is a direct translation of racing technology adapted to street use.

668
00:42:48,281 --> 00:42:50,460
A lot of sports cars or supercars.

669
00:42:50,480 --> 00:42:52,600
have really been developed out of racing.

670
00:42:53,480 --> 00:43:01,720
Our motorsports background has really enabled us to take almost 99% of what we've learned on the racetrack

671
00:43:01,721 --> 00:43:03,620
and put it into our street cars.

672
00:43:06,540 --> 00:43:09,660
Every S7 is custom built by hand.

673
00:43:09,960 --> 00:43:16,600
Its 560 horsepower, all aluminum V8, can hit top speeds and excess of 200 miles an hour.

674
00:43:18,100 --> 00:43:20,460
Its dynamic styling is made possible.

675
00:43:20,480 --> 00:43:22,960
by knowledge gained in the aerospace industry.

676
00:43:24,240 --> 00:43:27,480
Aerospace is using a lot of exotic materials.

677
00:43:27,780 --> 00:43:29,820
Those materials are making their way now

678
00:43:29,821 --> 00:43:31,940
into passenger and production cars.

679
00:43:32,340 --> 00:43:36,360
The S7's body, for example, is 100% carbon fiber.

680
00:43:37,100 --> 00:43:40,360
Carbon fiber is as strong as aluminum and ultralight weight,

681
00:43:40,740 --> 00:43:42,840
and it can be formed in ways metal can't.

682
00:43:43,420 --> 00:43:45,040
This advantage is more than cosmetic.

683
00:43:45,041 --> 00:43:48,820
It's all about keeping the car glued to the road at high speeds.

684
00:43:48,821 --> 00:43:52,360
Its 64 air vents enhanced the S-7's aerodynamics.

685
00:43:53,220 --> 00:43:59,660
The vents funnel the oncoming air around and through the car, reducing drag and improving downforce.

686
00:44:00,220 --> 00:44:07,700
We have achieved a very elaborate system of vents and ducts that allow a continuous airstream throughout the whole car.

687
00:44:08,200 --> 00:44:15,580
That starts at the front through what you see here with the vents and the ducting into an airfoil literally on the side of the car,

688
00:44:15,581 --> 00:44:18,800
which then in turn channels it into the engine compartment.

689
00:44:18,820 --> 00:44:25,820
and then back through the back of the car, giving us the best aerodynamics of any production car on the road today.

690
00:44:25,821 --> 00:44:32,820
With a price tag of around $400,000, the power of the S7 will remain in the hands of a few.

691
00:44:32,821 --> 00:44:40,820
But Steve believes you're getting a glimpse of the future of everyday automobiles when you feast your eyes on his supercar.

692
00:44:40,821 --> 00:44:45,820
What we're really watching and I think you'll see is that the use of this materials and the layout

693
00:44:45,821 --> 00:44:51,260
and the way it gets adapted from the racing will eventually make its way into everyday passenger cars.

694
00:44:51,800 --> 00:44:56,560
And it just is a matter of time and a matter of cost before it becomes more and more prevalent.

695
00:45:00,920 --> 00:45:06,280
In 1911, Ray Haroon won the Indianapolis 500 without the use of a riding mechanic.

696
00:45:06,860 --> 00:45:10,500
He utilized a new feature that allowed him to see what was happening behind him.

697
00:45:11,060 --> 00:45:15,220
Soon after, rearview mirrors became a standard item on passenger vehicles.

698
00:45:15,820 --> 00:45:19,040
Modern Marvel's Car Tech of the Future will return on the History Channel.

699
00:45:23,540 --> 00:45:26,680
The type of engines that will power cars in the future

700
00:45:26,681 --> 00:45:28,520
is a subject of much debate.

701
00:45:29,140 --> 00:45:32,040
Predictions are as varied as there are models of cars today.

702
00:45:32,600 --> 00:45:33,920
But one thing is for sure.

703
00:45:34,520 --> 00:45:37,780
We are on the verge of a new era every bit as revolutionary

704
00:45:37,781 --> 00:45:40,360
as the one that began the age of the automobile.

705
00:45:41,320 --> 00:45:45,120
Is it still going to be piston engine cars that are run on gasoline,

