00:45:45,121 --> 00:45:47,920
maybe we are going to end up going back to electrics.

707
00:45:48,660 --> 00:45:51,080
There's this new propulsion system called fuel cells.

708
00:45:51,200 --> 00:45:52,900
Maybe we're going to start turning to that now.

709
00:45:52,980 --> 00:45:55,700
So it's very much up in the air, just like it was back then.

710
00:45:55,900 --> 00:45:57,460
At the beginning of the 20th century,

711
00:45:58,060 --> 00:46:01,220
the technical future of the horseless carriage was undecided.

712
00:46:01,700 --> 00:46:03,440
There was no dominant technology.

713
00:46:04,240 --> 00:46:06,880
Early cars were powered in a variety of ways.

714
00:46:12,880 --> 00:46:14,820
Steam-powered railroad cars.

715
00:46:15,120 --> 00:46:16,500
It powered boats.

716
00:46:16,920 --> 00:46:18,140
Why couldn't it power cars?

717
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:21,820
Steam cars during their day were among the fastest cars.

718
00:46:22,560 --> 00:46:25,260
The steam car, you had maximum torque at zero RPM,

719
00:46:25,680 --> 00:46:30,960
so acceleration was lightning quick for 1900, 1905.

720
00:46:31,440 --> 00:46:34,720
The name synonymous with steam cars is the Stanley Steamer,

721
00:46:35,180 --> 00:46:38,440
created by Francis and Freeland Stanley in 1897.

722
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:44,200
A boiler provided enough pressure to drive a two-cylinder engine located onto the floor.

723
00:46:44,201 --> 00:46:50,080
The motor had only 16 moving parts and no spark plugs, transmission, clutch, or gear shift.

724
00:46:50,520 --> 00:46:54,020
The downside, it took at least half an hour to get up ahead of steam.

725
00:46:55,020 --> 00:46:58,920
In 1906, the Stanley Brothers built a streamlined speed car,

726
00:46:59,240 --> 00:47:03,040
powered by a 184 cubic inch twin piston steam engine.

727
00:47:03,520 --> 00:47:08,380
This compares to a 735 cubic inch V8 internal combustion engine.

728
00:47:09,180 --> 00:47:14,000
Driver Fred Marriott set a world land speed record of 127 miles an hour

729
00:47:14,001 --> 00:47:17,700
on Daytona Beach, which remained unbroken for another four years.

730
00:47:18,780 --> 00:47:21,200
The steam car lost out to gasoline engines,

731
00:47:21,700 --> 00:47:25,880
only after Cadillac's self-starter made starting those cars easier.

732
00:47:27,540 --> 00:47:30,680
Besides steam, electricity powered many automobiles,

733
00:47:31,220 --> 00:47:35,020
an electric car was quiet, clean running, and easy to handle.

734
00:47:35,820 --> 00:47:39,920
They became popular primarily with ladies of the day

735
00:47:39,921 --> 00:47:43,080
because you didn't have to get out and crank it to start it,

736
00:47:43,081 --> 00:47:47,120
or worry about lighting a steam boiler, you just got in,

737
00:47:47,540 --> 00:47:49,220
flicked a switch, pushed a lever,

738
00:47:49,520 --> 00:47:54,120
and you just were off, silently, effortlessly.

739
00:47:54,740 --> 00:47:58,720
And of course, there was the gasoline-powered internal combustion engine.

740
00:47:59,140 --> 00:48:03,940
Pound for pound, gasoline had more energy in it

741
00:48:03,941 --> 00:48:05,800
