00:49:30,780 --> 00:49:33,860
But gasoline power alone is not the only option.

762
00:49:34,580 --> 00:49:37,520
Recent technology has created a variety of new engines

763
00:49:37,521 --> 00:49:41,440
that may do an even better job of propelling the cars of tomorrow.

764
00:49:41,441 --> 00:49:45,000
There's a lot of debate today about what power trains will emerge tomorrow.

765
00:49:46,080 --> 00:49:50,800
Internal combustion engines, hybrid electric, diesel, fuel cells, solar.

766
00:49:51,240 --> 00:49:53,980
All of these are great new technologies that are emerging,

767
00:49:54,400 --> 00:49:56,300
that are making internal combustion engines better.

768
00:49:56,940 --> 00:49:59,920
The fact is, I believe it's going to be a matrix of these.

769
00:50:00,560 --> 00:50:05,200
This matrix of potential alternative power sources will take years to develop.

770
00:50:05,920 --> 00:50:10,580
But one version is already on the market, hybrid technology using gasoline.

771
00:50:10,581 --> 00:50:15,200
The hybrids, as we see them today, that really means two power sources in the car.

772
00:50:15,780 --> 00:50:18,920
What we're used to saying today is what they call the hybrid electric,

773
