Now through technology, we can do them in three years.

1175
01:14:55,340 --> 01:14:58,620
But you've got to bet the farm, like on a model, a billion dollars at one time

1176
01:14:58,621 --> 01:15:00,840
that three years from now, whatever car or truck you've built,

1177
01:15:01,340 --> 01:15:02,720
you'll be able to get your investment back.

1178
01:15:03,320 --> 01:15:04,080
So it's a crapshoot.

1179
01:15:04,380 --> 01:15:06,200
That's why, to me, it's a fascinating business.

1180
01:15:06,400 --> 01:15:09,760
It's not for everybody, not for the timid, believe me.

1181
01:15:13,320 --> 01:15:18,220
For that very reason, automakers rely on a very special kind of car,

1182
01:15:18,760 --> 01:15:21,640
one that helps both them and the public to decide

1183
01:15:21,641 --> 01:15:24,200
whether it's worth bringing a car like it to the market.

1184
01:15:24,920 --> 01:15:26,540
They're called concept cars.

1185
01:15:26,541 --> 01:15:32,780
Automobile companies unveil their latest concept car creations with great fanfare and showmanship.

1186
01:15:32,980 --> 01:15:40,120
These one-of-a-kind experimental vehicles are what every manufacturer uses to explore the future.

1187
01:15:40,760 --> 01:15:45,540
When we look at concept cars, in each one of them we see a fragment of the future.

1188
01:15:46,460 --> 01:15:56,520
And some more than others, because of the nature of the design, it's the role of the concept car to help guide scientists and engineers.

1189
01:15:56,540 --> 01:16:02,440
and designers as they bring all these elements together to build the future world we're going to enjoy.

1190
01:16:03,180 --> 01:16:08,920
The concept car is a necessary component in development of new technology.

1191
01:16:09,940 --> 01:16:14,000
And so when we test the concepts, we're testing not only the reaction,

1192
01:16:14,240 --> 01:16:16,260
but how they perform in the real world.

1193
01:16:16,460 --> 01:16:20,000
We can improve on that and make cars of the future even better.

1194
01:16:23,420 --> 01:16:26,520
The first stage of the process is a sketch on paper.

1195
01:16:26,540 --> 01:16:31,540
Any design starts off as an idea and a designer's mind.

1196
01:16:31,541 --> 01:16:34,540
So the first stage is to transfer it from the mind

1197
01:16:34,541 --> 01:16:38,540
into a medium which other people can share with them.

1198
01:16:38,541 --> 01:16:41,540
Next, the designers sculpt their concept in clay.

1199
01:16:41,541 --> 01:16:44,540
It's fine to be able to think in two dimensions,

1200
01:16:44,541 --> 01:16:47,540
but you have also to be able to think in three dimensions.

1201
01:16:47,541 --> 01:16:49,540
So the next phase, fundamentally,

1202
01:16:49,541 --> 01:16:53,540
is to convert those sketches into a three-dimensional representation.

1203
01:16:53,541 --> 01:16:59,860
This traditional process can also now be done with computers.

1204
01:17:00,480 --> 01:17:04,840
With the computers and stuff, you can really expand your whole vocabulary of design.

1205
01:17:04,980 --> 01:17:10,140
You can really explore new fundamental concepts that will really change the way we move around.

1206
01:17:10,640 --> 01:17:12,900
Car designer of the future is really going to be a concept engineer.

1207
01:17:13,140 --> 01:17:15,440
He's really going to have to be conscious of the package,

1208
01:17:15,800 --> 01:17:18,760
conscious of how people sit in vehicles, how they interact with the vehicles.

1209
01:17:19,200 --> 01:17:22,840
With computer technology, that process opens up a whole new world to us.

1210
01:17:22,841 --> 01:17:30,000
To move from a sketch on piece of paper to a hard model design to production in 12 to 18 months, it's a radical thing.

1211
01:17:30,820 --> 01:17:33,400
A concept can be a technological study.

1212
01:17:33,820 --> 01:17:40,640
A concept can be a pre-production vehicle that is only calling attention to a vehicle that we will eventually put into production.

1213
01:17:41,240 --> 01:17:43,460
Or a concept can be a dream.

1214
01:17:43,860 --> 01:17:47,560
And we called those years ago dream cars, and that's exactly what they are.

1215
01:17:47,860 --> 01:17:52,820
And those are probably the purest form of sheer fantasy that an auto designer can.

1216
01:17:52,840 --> 01:17:53,899
can come up with.

1217
01:17:53,900 --> 01:17:58,880
General Motors was the first company that really devoted a department to styling

1218
01:17:58,881 --> 01:17:59,581
vehicles.

1219
01:17:59,582 --> 01:18:03,480
And it was really Alfred Sloan, who was the president of General Motors back in

1220
01:18:03,481 --> 01:18:04,328
1926, 1927.

1221
01:18:04,329 --> 01:18:10,960
Alfred Sloan believed in the future that design would play a major role in influencing

1222
01:18:10,961 --> 01:18:12,795
people to buy vehicles.

1223
01:18:12,796 --> 01:18:17,660
Sloan began the art and color section of GM and hired a young

1224
01:18:17,661 --> 01:18:22,820
Californian named Harley Earl to run it. Earl had earned a reputation for

1225
01:18:22,840 --> 01:18:25,560
building custom cars for Hollywood movie stars.

1226
01:18:26,280 --> 01:18:31,960
His first car for GM was the 1927 LaSalle, a fast, sharp-looking two-seater.

1227
01:18:32,600 --> 01:18:36,660
With its flowing lines and low-profile, the new car created a sensation.

1228
01:18:37,540 --> 01:18:43,380
In 1938, Earl created what would come to be considered the first corporate car built solely

1229
01:18:43,381 --> 01:18:45,520
as an experiment in style and function.

1230
01:18:46,160 --> 01:18:47,680
The Buick Y-job.

1231
01:18:49,520 --> 01:18:52,820
The Y-job featured retractable soft-top roof.

1232
01:18:52,840 --> 01:18:56,140
power windows and concealed headlights.

1233
01:18:59,000 --> 01:19:03,620
In 1950, Earl's team unveiled what is widely considered to be

1234
01:19:03,621 --> 01:19:06,420
one of the most outstanding concept cars ever built.

1235
01:19:06,980 --> 01:19:09,100
The Jet Fighter inspired Lesaber.

1236
01:19:09,960 --> 01:19:16,600
I think you can see how this car has been influenced, you know, by the jet age, the emerging jet age.

1237
01:19:16,740 --> 01:19:20,220
You know, there's an air intake and a front like a jet air intake.

1238
01:19:20,221 --> 01:19:22,820
And what's really cool about that is the headlights swore.

1239
01:19:22,840 --> 01:19:26,140
around, so they're hidden and they swivel around in the front air intake.

1240
01:19:27,140 --> 01:19:33,140
The LeSaber had heated seats and a rain detector to automatically put up the convertible top.

1241
01:19:33,840 --> 01:19:40,340
The interior continued the fighter jet motif, and the LeSaber was the first car to have a wraparound windshield,

1242
01:19:40,940 --> 01:19:42,380
which all cars now have.

1243
01:19:42,740 --> 01:19:47,500
It was just a lot of technology in this vehicle for the early 50, so it wasn't just a great looker.

1244
01:19:47,940 --> 01:19:50,040
I mean, this car was all about the future.

1245
01:19:50,041 --> 01:19:55,080
Taking the concept car to the outer limits in 1954,

1246
01:19:55,960 --> 01:19:58,780
Earl introduced the first of his firebird cars.

1247
01:19:59,480 --> 01:20:01,280
This was a car that was turbine powered.

1248
01:20:01,980 --> 01:20:03,420
It sat one person.

1249
01:20:03,620 --> 01:20:05,560
It looked like a fuselage with wings.

1250
01:20:12,020 --> 01:20:16,960
Earl followed the firebird one with the even wilder firebirds two and three.

1251
01:20:17,540 --> 01:20:19,180
Like many concept cars,

1252
01:20:19,181 --> 01:20:23,120
The firebirds were built to give their parent company, bragging rights.

1253
01:20:25,160 --> 01:20:29,480
Harley Earle didn't have that car built to test public reaction

1254
01:20:29,481 --> 01:20:32,120
to the idea of it going into production.

1255
01:20:32,520 --> 01:20:36,900
He had it built to tease the public, to say, look at General Motors, look what we're doing.

1256
01:20:37,380 --> 01:20:40,660
We are thinking so far ahead of everybody else.

1257
01:20:41,040 --> 01:20:44,740
Just think of what kind of technology is embodied in your production car

1258
01:20:44,741 --> 01:20:46,780
if we're thinking this far ahead already.

1259
01:20:46,781 --> 01:20:56,217
The optimism of the 50s, to use one example, is what actually created those fabulous cars with tail fins and afterburner tail lamps and gobs of chrome all over them,

1260
01:20:56,218 --> 01:21:00,220
because we really thought that that's what the future would look like.

1261
01:21:04,020 --> 01:21:13,357
Though none of these fantastic concept cars ever saw the assembly line, they helped automakers and the public to find the direction of car design for the fast

1262
01:21:13,358 --> 01:21:14,480
approaching future.

1263
01:21:14,980 --> 01:21:15,840
The result?

1264
01:21:16,780 --> 01:21:18,920
new generation of concept cars.

1265
01:21:19,560 --> 01:21:20,820
Today's concept cars

1266
01:21:20,821 --> 01:21:22,880
are no less enthralling, offering

1267
01:21:22,881 --> 01:21:24,940
new dreams for a new age.

1268
01:21:25,080 --> 01:21:26,980
At least so far in this century, it's all about

1269
01:21:26,981 --> 01:21:28,680
choice. And people want

1270
01:21:28,681 --> 01:21:30,620
adventure, they want status,

1271
01:21:30,920 --> 01:21:32,740
they want retrospective design,

1272
01:21:32,860 --> 01:21:34,900
they want optimism, they want rebellion.

1273
01:21:35,520 --> 01:21:36,780
Your future is your

1274
01:21:36,781 --> 01:21:38,980
choice, and we're going to deliver that on a plate

1275
01:21:38,981 --> 01:21:41,000
that allows you to pick from a spectrum

1276
01:21:41,001 --> 01:21:42,920
of possibilities because the whole

1277
01:21:42,921 --> 01:21:44,900
point of design is for us to try to

1278
01:21:44,901 --> 01:21:45,760
make your life better.

1279
01:21:46,780 --> 01:21:52,580
The role of science fiction will also have a strong influence in predicting what cars will look like in the future.

1280
01:21:53,080 --> 01:21:58,580
If you want something with an impact that makes people think, wow, that is really different,

1281
01:21:59,020 --> 01:22:02,080
then you really have to radically change the proportions.

1282
01:22:02,580 --> 01:22:09,460
Designer Harold Belker did just that when he conceived of a sports car for Stephen Spielberg's futuristic film Minority Report.

1283
01:22:10,240 --> 01:22:14,440
Belker believes this is what Alexis may look like in the year 2054.

1284
01:22:14,441 --> 01:22:19,040
You ask yourself, what would it take to really push it over the top?

1285
01:22:19,041 --> 01:22:24,040
So the answer was that I shifted the whole proportion so far forward

1286
01:22:24,041 --> 01:22:27,940
that a lot of people, when they saw the car, thought it was actually going the other way,

1287
01:22:27,941 --> 01:22:30,440
which is, in a way, a great success,

1288
01:22:30,441 --> 01:22:35,940
because you really have introduced a new shape that people are not comfortable with.

1289
01:22:35,941 --> 01:22:42,940
With that shape, we're going to see probably a lot more designs in that direction.

1290
01:22:42,941 --> 01:22:46,980
And then at some point, there are going to be people who introduce completely different shapes.

1291
01:22:47,760 --> 01:22:53,500
Science fiction has pretty steadily predicted actual technological progress.

1292
01:22:54,720 --> 01:23:00,800
Sid Mead is a former car designer who has visualized the far distant future in films such as Tron,

1293
01:23:01,340 --> 01:23:04,080
2010, Alien, and Blade Runner.

1294
01:23:05,180 --> 01:23:12,040
Consider this view of car technology of the future in Mead's illustration known as the Silver Coach.

1295
01:23:12,940 --> 01:23:15,240
So you arrive in this vehicle.

1296
01:23:15,980 --> 01:23:19,080
Now you've got high technology because there's one wheel in the front,

1297
01:23:19,480 --> 01:23:26,560
and that big black sphere in back is the traction, the motive power, the steering, and suspension, everything.

1298
01:23:27,120 --> 01:23:32,440
And it literally is floating in this loop that it's trapped in by electromagnetic attraction.

1299
01:23:32,980 --> 01:23:37,240
Because it's a sphere, you can roll the thing down around in a circle and park it.

1300
01:23:37,660 --> 01:23:40,000
You can go forward, back, stop, start.

1301
01:23:40,001 --> 01:23:42,920
So it's an idea for a very elaborate kind of view.

1302
01:23:42,940 --> 01:23:46,240
vehicle and you can just see the two people in back getting out.

1303
01:23:47,040 --> 01:23:51,000
They've just arrived and you can make anything of it that you like.

1304
01:23:55,120 --> 01:24:06,480
The 1956 Firebird 2 concept car was part of a plan for a controlled access electronic highway system.

1305
01:24:07,160 --> 01:24:12,700
The roadway would have embedded wires for cars to pick up the signal and steer the vehicle automatically.

1306
01:24:12,940 --> 01:24:17,420
Modern Marbles Car Take of the Future will return on the History Channel.

1307
01:24:19,180 --> 01:24:27,240
The ultimate car technology of the future has to be a vehicle with all the comforts of a car without the constraints of the ground.

1308
01:24:27,740 --> 01:24:29,500
The so-called flying car.

1309
01:24:30,040 --> 01:24:31,740
Flying cars already exist.

1310
01:24:32,280 --> 01:24:34,480
Flying cars were developed in the 1960s.

1311
01:24:34,481 --> 01:24:41,960
The first flying car to be certified by the Civil Aeronautics Administration, the predecessor of the FAAA, was the Airfibian.

1312
01:24:41,961 --> 01:24:44,060
A plane adapted for the road.

1313
01:24:44,620 --> 01:24:48,080
Its six-cylinder engine could fly at 120 miles per hour

1314
01:24:48,081 --> 01:24:50,260
and drive at 50 miles per hour.

1315
01:24:51,000 --> 01:24:55,640
In the 1960s, the AeroCar gained notoriety flying on TV shows.

1316
01:24:56,140 --> 01:24:59,780
The cockpit was a fiberglass shell based on a geometro car.

1317
01:25:00,340 --> 01:25:04,180
A 10-foot-long drive shaft connected the engine to a pusher propeller.

1318
01:25:04,820 --> 01:25:07,640
Even though this was the most successful flying car ever built,

1319
01:25:08,140 --> 01:25:10,840
lack of venture capital kept mass production on the ground.

1320
01:25:10,841 --> 01:25:15,340
The AeroCar was the last rotable aircraft to receive FAA approval.

1321
01:25:16,660 --> 01:25:20,760
Since the 1980s, Carl Moller and his company, Moller International,

1322
01:25:21,160 --> 01:25:23,060
has been working on hovercraft technology.

1323
01:25:23,740 --> 01:25:27,660
This early model uses eight rotary engines generating 400 horsepower.

1324
01:25:28,440 --> 01:25:32,080
Rotary engines are giant fans pushing air downward to create lift.

1325
01:25:33,540 --> 01:25:39,600
Mueller's new experimental M-400 Skycar uses four rotary engines generating 720 horsepower.

1326
01:25:39,601 --> 01:25:43,680
The engines can rotate after liftoff to create forward thrust.

1327
01:25:44,400 --> 01:25:47,960
Top speed is projected to be 380 miles an hour.

1328
01:25:49,040 --> 01:25:52,600
This computer-generated hovercraft from macro industries

1329
01:25:52,601 --> 01:25:56,160
shows what a personal hovercraft of the future might look like.

1330
01:25:56,800 --> 01:25:59,520
Its flight characteristics are very similar to a helicopter.

1331
01:26:00,160 --> 01:26:02,540
But while cross-country commuting might be practical,

1332
01:26:03,120 --> 01:26:05,220
grocery shopping might be a lot more complicated.

1333
01:26:05,920 --> 01:26:08,420
We have problems with drivers who can't look right and left.

1334
01:26:08,421 --> 01:26:12,220
Think about if they have to be in the air and look right, left, and now up and down.

1335
01:26:12,660 --> 01:26:15,080
I think eventually the day will come where technology will catch up,

1336
01:26:15,140 --> 01:26:19,040
and we will have a flying car that popular science and all those people in the 50s really wanted to see.

1337
01:26:19,860 --> 01:26:25,720
Every year, more and more serious scientists assume that we will figure out why gravity works,

1338
01:26:25,780 --> 01:26:29,060
we really don't know still, and how to control it.

1339
01:26:29,600 --> 01:26:33,500
So you've got to have a capacitor, like a gravity capacitor of some kind,

1340
01:26:33,960 --> 01:26:38,400
and then carefully control the energy going into the capacity,

1341
01:26:38,420 --> 01:26:41,980
and coming back out like you do in any version of electronics

1342
01:26:41,981 --> 01:26:45,980
in order to control gravity, and I think we'll do it.

1343
01:26:48,340 --> 01:26:52,600
Today, the future of car technology is taking shape at schools,

1344
01:26:52,960 --> 01:26:56,180
such as the Art Center College of Design in Pasadena, California.

1345
01:26:56,680 --> 01:27:00,720
For 70 years, this campus has educated more named car designers

1346
01:27:00,721 --> 01:27:02,560
than any other place in the world.

1347
01:27:03,300 --> 01:27:06,820
Here, the students must master the various skills they'll need

1348
01:27:06,821 --> 01:27:08,400
to design the cars of tomorrow,

1349
01:27:08,420 --> 01:27:11,980
a role that will grow in importance in the years ahead.

1350
01:27:12,280 --> 01:27:15,240
There's some huge opportunities for the car industry in future

1351
01:27:15,241 --> 01:27:19,180
to think more about a much greater array of vehicles

1352
01:27:19,181 --> 01:27:22,460
that any particular customer might choose to use

1353
01:27:22,461 --> 01:27:24,380
according to what their journey is going to be.

1354
01:27:24,660 --> 01:27:27,780
And we're encouraging our students to start thinking a lot more

1355
01:27:27,781 --> 01:27:31,760
about what kinds of vehicles should we be designing

1356
01:27:31,761 --> 01:27:36,060
which will enable people still to have the freedom of use of the automobile

1357
01:27:36,061 --> 01:27:38,360
without some of the drawbacks.

1358
01:27:38,420 --> 01:27:45,220
Michael Rinaldi's project is to create a car that could help alleviate traffic congestion problems in major cities.

1359
01:27:45,640 --> 01:27:48,340
Futuristic thing about my vehicle is that it's self-driving.

1360
01:27:48,640 --> 01:27:50,380
It's satellite GPS control.

1361
01:27:51,060 --> 01:27:59,360
We're about two to three years away from having a vehicle that can legitimately run around in an environment by itself being controlled by GPS satellites.

1362
01:27:59,600 --> 01:28:06,480
Being that it's self-guided, the vehicle can literally drop you off at a terminal in front of the building, in front of a school, such as like a theme park ride,

1363
01:28:06,481 --> 01:28:09,780
and they can run off by themselves and go park themselves.

1364
01:28:09,920 --> 01:28:11,720
You never have to go find your car again if you don't have to.

1365
01:28:12,720 --> 01:28:15,700
If there's any trend in the history of car technology,

1366
01:28:16,220 --> 01:28:19,720
it's that we'll keep one eye on the past while looking towards the future.

1367
01:28:20,100 --> 01:28:23,680
I think the important thing about technology is it changes because lifestyles change.

1368
01:28:24,560 --> 01:28:28,540
And if you don't keep up with it, you lose sort of important segments of the market.

1369
01:28:28,920 --> 01:28:33,200
There have been huge strides in efficiency in terms of emissions and fuel economy

1370
01:28:33,201 --> 01:28:36,460
in the cars that we drive today compared to those of the...

1371
01:28:36,480 --> 01:28:38,640
even 10 years ago, never mind 30 or 40.

1372
01:28:39,160 --> 01:28:41,960
So efficiency, emissions control,

1373
01:28:42,320 --> 01:28:43,960
those are clearly trends that are going to continue.

1374
01:28:44,240 --> 01:28:46,600
What we're trying to do is to build vehicles

1375
01:28:46,601 --> 01:28:48,720
that absolutely have no trade-offs,

1376
01:28:49,420 --> 01:28:52,580
where you have safety, environmental responsibility,

1377
01:28:53,380 --> 01:28:57,240
emotion, fun to drive, easy, convenient, luxurious.

1378
01:28:58,260 --> 01:29:01,560
Customers of today no longer want just one of those,

1379
01:29:01,860 --> 01:29:03,060
they want all of them.

1380
01:29:03,160 --> 01:29:06,260
You can't always get all those things out of the same package

1381
01:29:06,261 --> 01:29:11,320
at the same time, but you can have a selection, just a keyboard on the dashboard, to decide

1382
01:29:11,321 --> 01:29:15,680
how you want your car to be at any given instant, whether you want it to have high performance

1383
01:29:15,681 --> 01:29:16,860
or high economy.

1384
01:29:17,280 --> 01:29:22,440
It's extremely difficult to say what kinds of cars we're going to be driving in the future,

1385
01:29:22,900 --> 01:29:27,500
but whatever they are, you know they're going to be very aerodynamic, you know that they're

1386
01:29:27,501 --> 01:29:35,040
going to be very clean, they're going to use materials that can be recycled, and they're

1387
01:29:35,041 --> 01:29:37,200
going to look really, really cool.

1388
01:29:38,200 --> 01:29:43,860
The automobile's rich history has proven time and time again that the only limit on its

1389
01:29:43,861 --> 01:29:46,420
future is man's ability to dream.

